{"author":{"id":"127a58c7f014820991be95805df42525db12c92e2d7319d04d4df105a9aa3444"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1788184969,"nonce":"lsZ4x4xNw4rK0/6KctY+U5qpJSo=","message":"CLOSED — 139 of 147, all four acceptance bullets demonstrated in ONE run, zero\nred errors. Merged fast-forward to main at 7996fe6.\n\nThe 8 remaining failures are ALL the same blocked gate and are tracked as\ne8f2c32: 4.7a-e and 5.1a-c use work priorities 1 and 2, `work-priorities`\ncorrectly refuses those with manual priorities off, and nothing in the verb\nsurface can turn manual priorities on. Not a 3.4 defect and not fixable inside\n3.4 — they will be exercised when e8f2c32 ships. Everything else passes.\n\nBULLETS, all four, one run\n\n- 1 draft + move + undraft, drafted pawn HOLDS: 27 checks, 0 failures.\n- 2 `prioritize haul` hauls it NEXT: the job report reads \"hauling steel x75 to\n  Stockpile zone 1.\"\n- 3 policy-driven re-dress: wearing the parka within the FIRST 5000-tick window,\n  cold insulation up, disallowed apparel removed.\n- 4 surgery performed by a doctor under advance: bill gone, `Anesthetic` hediff\n  on the patient.\n\nPlus 5.3 — the disabled-work-type red-error pre-check — exercised for the FIRST\ntime. It had been a NOTE in every prior run because no actor happened to have a\ndisabled work type. It passes: the call is refused, the gate is named, and no\nred error is logged.\n\nTHE DEFECT THIS FOUND AND FIXED (0a5085d)\n\n`warden {mode:\"AttemptRecruit\", recruitable:true}` returned ok:true with the\nmode silently unapplied: the mode gate ran `ModeHidden` -\u003e `Recruitable` two\nlevers before `recruitable` was written. Order is now clear -\u003e recruitable -\u003e\nmode -\u003e enable -\u003e disable -\u003e slave_mode -\u003e convert_to, which is also how the tab\nbehaves (tick Recruitable, the radio list redraws, then pick). 5.16b passes.\n\nFOUR RUNS TO GET HERE, AND THE FIXTURE WAS THE COST EVERY TIME: 130 -\u003e 133 -\u003e\n138 -\u003e 139. Not one of those steps was a code fix except the warden one.\n\nFIXTURE REQUIREMENTS THE RUN-SHEET DOES NOT LIST, and every one cost a run\n\n`accept/3.4-pawn-orders.md`'s fixture table says \"at least 2 visible colonists\".\nThat is not sufficient. It also needs:\n\n- **An actor capable of Hauling and Doctor.** A colonist with Hauling disabled\n  fails bullet 2 with six checks and no obvious cause — the only clue is a NOTE\n  (\"work type disabled for this pawn: hauling\"). Add it to the table.\n- **Enough doctor capacity.** With two colonists where the patient cannot\n  doctor, the surgery never happens inside 20000 ticks and bullet 4 fails.\n- **Rested pawns.** Bullet 3's re-dress needs a free think tick;\n  JobGiver_OptimizeApparel never runs on a pawn that goes to sleep, and the\n  first run lost bullet 3 that way.\n- **A stockpile sited AWAY from where colonists idle.** Phase 2 spawns the steel\n  at `pawn:A`; if the zone is on top of them it lands already-stored and there\n  is no haul job.\n\n**AND THE ACTOR IS NOT DETERMINISTIC.** `pawns {filter:\"colonist\"}` returned a\nDIFFERENT order for the same colony across two calls in one session — a pawn\nspawn reordered it. Phase 0 takes `roster[0]` as the actor and `roster[1]` as\nthe patient, so the acceptance is keyed on an unstable index. I worked around it\nby making every colonist in the fixture suitable, which is a workaround, not a\nfix. Either `pawns` should return a stable order or phase 0 should SELECT an\nactor by capability. Worth a decision before more position-keyed acceptance is\nwritten; it will bite 3.6 and 4.3 the same way.\n\nBENCH FIXTURE, saved as autostart.rws (tick 58205)\n\nQuicktest map, 4 colonists all at 100% health with needs topped up and NONE with\nHauling or Doctor disabled, a 144-cell stockpile with 115 free sited 16+ cells\nclear of the pawns, research bench, 32 startable projects, Anesthetize addable.\nThe surgery patient from the last run was healed rather than left bleeding in\nthe save. This is the fixture the next spec should start from.","files":null}]}